# legs/adult/loco/far: the FAR leg of the adult side walk and run, a whole leg on its own part (P2b motion proto2, 2026-10-21;
# ROLLOUT ADULT-RIG polish (2026-10-22): run6 (flight, base and woman) the trailing far thigh's y -9 row ends on its own
# outline at u +1 (no stray pixel under the lead thigh), a pixel of grass between the thighs (std.pxm's header).
# the owner: "whatever leg is covered by the front leg ... that leg is also the same size as the front leg"). The legs
# layer draws this part first (z -1) and legs/adult/loco/std (the near leg, z 0) over it, so the far leg is drawn full
# width (the idle's 5 px leg, the same capsule as the near leg: 5 px across the bone at any angle) and only the pixels
# the near leg covers are hidden. Its value: the idle's far leg (cloth 3 then 2, leather h then g, the first visible
# interior pixel of each row lit), never one flat dark. It also carries what both legs share under the hem: the seat row
# and the hips filled out to the idle's hip width. Side views only (R, L) of the walk and run keys; the front and back
# views of the shared keys are empty (std draws both legs there). Generated with std (its header says how); never by hand.
# (proto2 i2) the run keys' legs are drawn whole (std's header: they may fold); where the far leg would show beside the
# near leg as a 1-2 px sliver its row slides under the near leg instead (the width as drawn kept, never narrower).
# (proto3 i1, 2026-10-21) every far leg redrawn with std (its header): the thigh's top under the hips, >= 4 px across.
# (proto2 i3) the run keys redrawn with std (its header: a circular leg path, both boots 2 px up in flight); every run
# leg drawn whole by legkit6 (the boot owns only its own pixels), the far leg the near leg's capsule, full width.
use person
body adult
role legs std
layer legs
z -1
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_adult
tags boots-stamped

